        "step_anchor": "step-6",
        "title": "Subtraction With Larger Numbers",
        "key_prerequisites": [],
        "has_content_in_snapshot": true,
        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>It is impractical to use number lines to subtract large numbers. </p>",
            "readable_text": "It is impractical to use number lines to subtract large numbers.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>However, a neat trick makes subtracting a positive number from a smaller positive number very easy!</p>",
            "readable_text": "However, a neat trick makes subtracting a positive number from a smaller positive number very easy!",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>As an example, let&#x27;s consider the following subtraction problem:</p>",
            "readable_text": "As an example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: {\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Since <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 68]</span> is larger than <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 37,]</span> the answer <em>must be negative</em>.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Since [MATH: 68] is larger than [MATH: 37,] the answer must be negative.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We start by solving an easier problem: subtracting the numbers <em>in the reverse order</em>. In our case, the reverse problem is\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We start by solving an easier problem: subtracting the numbers in the reverse order. In our case, the reverse problem is\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Next, we carry out the subtraction:</p>",
            "readable_text": "Next, we carry out the subtraction:",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: 6|8; \u2212|3|7; 3|1]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: 6|8; \u2212|3|7; 3|1]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>So, we have</p>",
            "readable_text": "So, we have",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}} = 31.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[MATH: {\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}} = 31.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>However, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above. </p>",
            "readable_text": "However, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Therefore, we conclude that\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: {\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}} = -31.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Therefore, we conclude that\n[MATH: {\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}} = -31.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>And that&#x27;s it! </p>",
            "readable_text": "And that's it!",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Let&#x27;s use the same idea to subtract two three-digit numbers.</p>",
            "readable_text": "Let's use the same idea to subtract two three-digit numbers.",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Content:\nIt is impractical to use number lines to subtract large numbers.\n\nContent:\nHowever, a neat trick makes subtracting a positive number from a smaller positive number very easy!\n\nContent:\nAs an example, let's consider the following subtraction problem:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: {\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}}]\n\nContent:\nSince [MATH: 68] is larger than [MATH: 37,] the answer must be negative.\n\nContent:\nWe start by solving an easier problem: subtracting the numbers in the reverse order. In our case, the reverse problem is\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}}.]\n\nContent:\nNext, we carry out the subtraction:\n\nContent:\n[MATH: 6|8; \u2212|3|7; 3|1]\n\nContent:\nSo, we have\n\nContent:\n[MATH: {\\color{blue}{68}} - {\\color{red}{37}} = 31.]\n\nContent:\nHowever, since our answer must be negative, we need to change the sign of the answer above.\n\nContent:\nTherefore, we conclude that\n[MATH: {\\color{red}{37}} - {\\color{blue}{68}} = -31.]\n\nContent:\nAnd that's it!\n\nContent:\nLet's use the same idea to subtract two three-digit numbers."
      },
